{0 Libdictenstein for OCaml}

This package provides native dictionaries and trie maps for exact lookup,
snapshot-consistent iteration, set algebra, and approximate-search providers.
The public module is {!module:Vinary_tree_libdictenstein}. Its resource can be
passed to the independently packaged liblevenshtein OCaml binding.

{1 First dictionary}

Create a mutable Unicode-scalar DynamicDAWG and close it deterministically.
An entry can be present without a value; [None] is not an absence marker.

{[
module D = Vinary_tree_libdictenstein

let example () =
  let words = D.dynamic_dawg () in
  Fun.protect ~finally:(fun () -> D.close words) (fun () ->
    ignore (D.put_many words [| ("cat", Some 1L); ("cot", None) |]);
    let value = D.get words "cot" in
    assert (value.found && value.value = None);
    D.fold_entries words ~init:[]
      ~f:(fun seen entry -> entry.key :: seen))
]}

{1 Selecting a backend and domain}

{!Vinary_tree_libdictenstein.dynamic_dawg} supports byte, Unicode-scalar,
and unsigned-64 token domains and accepts mutation. A double-array trie
is read-optimized and immutable after construction. SCDAWG adds substring
queries. Persistent ARTrie and vocabulary backends provide checkpoint/reopen.
Check {!Vinary_tree_libdictenstein.capabilities} before invoking optional
operations. The OCaml PathMap and typed suffix-index constructors currently
report unsupported; they are not substitutes for the other backends.

Text keys are OCaml [string] values validated as UTF-8 in the Unicode domain.
Bytes keys may contain arbitrary octets. Unsigned-64 token keys are OCaml
[int64 array] values whose bits are preserved, including values above the
signed range. An optional value [Some 0L] is distinct from [None].

{1 Snapshots and algebra}

{!Vinary_tree_libdictenstein.with_entries_seq} scopes a lazy ordered sequence
to one immutable revision and closes its native cursor even if the callback
raises or returns early. Its entries are owned OCaml values. Do not return
the lazy sequence from the callback. The eager reducer
{!Vinary_tree_libdictenstein.fold_entries} offers the same snapshot law.

Union, intersection, left difference, and symmetric difference each capture
one immutable revision of both inputs and return a new mutable DynamicDAWG.
Shared keys use an explicit optional-value policy. Close the result:

{[
let union_size left right =
  let joined = D.union ~value_merge:D.Lattice_join left right in
  Fun.protect ~finally:(fun () -> D.close joined)
    (fun () -> D.length joined)
]}

{1 Errors and resource handoff}

Native status failures raise OCaml [Failure] carrying a copied diagnostic;
this facade does not expose a typed status exception. The producer's
{!Vinary_tree_libdictenstein.resource} is retained independently by a
consumer, so closing the original dictionary does not invalidate an
already-captured query. For exact status, domain, and capability contracts,
see the native ABI reference:
https://github.com/vinary-tree/libdictenstein/blob/master/docs/bindings/c-abi-reference.md
